<body>
<div class="container">

<!-- ====== HEADER ====== -->
<div class="header">
  <h1>🔌 IRLZ44N Wireless TX Coil Driver</h1>
  <p>Complete Build Guide — ESP32 @ 1 MHz, IRLZ44N direct drive, 18–20 AWG coils, 5–12W</p>
  <p style="margin-top:6px;"><strong>RX Side:</strong> Battery + filament LED only (no extra components)</p>
</div>

<!-- ====== 1. OVERVIEW ====== -->
<section>
<h2>1. System Overview</h2>

<h3>How It Works</h3>
<ol>
  <li><b>ESP32</b> generates a <b>1 MHz PWM</b> signal on GPIO 2</li>
  <li>Signal goes through <b>100Ω resistor</b> to Gate of <b>IRLZ44N</b> (logic-level MOSFET)</li>
  <li>IRLZ44N turns <b>fully ON at 3.3V</b> — <i>no gate driver needed</i></li>
  <li>MOSFET switches the <b>LC tank</b> (coil + capacitor) at 1 MHz</li>
  <li>At resonance, the coil generates a <b>strong 1 MHz magnetic field</b></li>
  <li>The <b>battery + LED loop</b> on the RX side acts as a single-turn receiver coil</li>
  <li>Faraday induction adds an AC voltage → LED gets <b>brighter</b></li>
</ol>

<h3>Key Advantages of IRLZ44N</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>MOSFET</th><th>Type</th><th>Vgs(th)</th><th>Fully ON at</th><th>Direct from ESP32?</th></tr>
  <tr><td><b>IRLZ44N</b> ✅</td><td>Logic-level N-Ch</td><td>1–2 V</td><td><b>3.3–5 V</b></td><td><b>✅ YES</b></td></tr>
  <tr><td>IRFZ44N</td><td>Standard N-Ch</td><td>2–4 V</td><td>~10 V</td><td>❌ Needs extra driver</td></tr>
  <tr><td>IRF520</td><td>Standard N-Ch</td><td>2–4 V</td><td>~10 V</td><td>❌ Needs extra driver</td></tr>
</table>
</section>

<!-- ====== 2. COMPLETE BOM ====== -->
<section>
<h2>2. Bill of Materials (BOM)</h2>

<h3>2.1 Essential Components</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>#</th><th>Item</th><th>Spec / Value</th><th>Qty</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
  <tr><td>1</td><td>ESP32 Dev Board</td><td>Any (NodeMCU-32S, DOIT, etc.)</td><td>1</td><td>USB powered</td></tr>
  <tr><td>2</td><td><b>IRLZ44N</b> MOSFET</td><td>TO-220, 55V / 47A, Logic-level</td><td>1</td><td>⭐ The key part</td></tr>
  <tr><td>3</td><td>100Ω Resistor</td><td>¼W carbon film</td><td>1</td><td>Gate series resistor</td></tr>
  <tr><td>4</td><td>10kΩ Resistor</td><td>¼W carbon film</td><td>1</td><td>Gate pull-down to GND</td></tr>
  <tr><td>5</td><td>Tuning Capacitor</td><td>See Section 4 for value</td><td>1+</td><td>Polypropylene or C0G/NP0 ceramic</td></tr>
  <tr><td>6</td><td>TX Coil</td><td>18 or 20 AWG magnet wire</td><td>1</td><td>See Section 4 for specs</td></tr>
  <tr><td>7</td><td>Non-polarized Filament LED</td><td>AC/DC compatible</td><td>1</td><td>Two reverse-parallel dies</td></tr>
  <tr><td>8</td><td>Battery (RX side)</td><td>3.7–12V NiMH / NiCd / Alkaline</td><td>1</td><td>⚠️ NO Li-ion without BMS!</td></tr>
  <tr><td>9</td><td>Hook-up wire (RX loop)</td><td>22 AWG, ~30 cm</td><td>1</td><td>For battery ↔ LED connections</td></tr>
  <tr><td>10</td><td>USB Cable</td><td>Micro-USB or USB-C</td><td>1</td><td>Data + power for ESP32</td></tr>
  <tr><td>11</td><td>External DC Power Supply</td><td><b>5–12V DC, ≥1–3A</b></td><td>1</td><td>See Section 7 for sizing</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>2.2 Optional but Recommended</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Item</th><th>Spec</th><th>Why</th></tr>
  <tr><td>100 µF Electrolytic Cap</td><td>25V or 50V</td><td>Bulk decoupling on the supply input — reduces ripple, stabilizes MOSFET switching</td></tr>
  <tr><td>0.1 µF (100 nF) Ceramic Cap</td><td>50V, any dielectric</td><td>High-frequency bypass — place close to MOSFET Drain/Source</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Trimmer Capacitor</td><td>50–200 pF ceramic trimmer</td><td>Fine-tune resonance by turning a screw — no need to swap caps</td></tr>
  <tr><td>1N4148 Fast Diode</td><td>Standard signal diode</td><td>Flyback protection across the coil (Drain to +V, cathode to +V)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Heatsink</td><td>TO-220 clip-on</td><td>IRLZ44N gets warm at 5–12W — highly recommended for runs &gt;30s</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Breadboard + Jumpers</td><td>Half-size + M-M wires</td><td>For prototyping before soldering</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Multimeter</td><td>Digital, any</td><td>Continuity checks, voltage measurements</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Oscilloscope (if available)</td><td>Any 10MHz+ scope</td><td>See the resonance peak directly — tune for max Vpp across coil</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="callout good">
<strong>⭐ Minimum Viable Parts:</strong> ESP32 + IRLZ44N + 100Ω + 10kΩ + tuning cap + coil + battery + LED. That's it.
</div>
</section>

<!-- ====== 3. PIN CONFIG & SCHEMATIC ====== -->
<section>
<h2>3. Pin Configuration &amp; Full Schematic</h2>

<h3>3.1 IRLZ44N Pinout (TO-220)</h3>
<div class="diagram">
         ┌─────────────────────┐
         │                     │
         │     IRLZ44N         │
         │                     │
         │  Left    Center   Right │
         │  Gate    Drain    Source│
         │   (G)     (D)      (S) │
         │                     │
         └────────┬────┬───────┘
                  │    │
                  │    └── Metal tab = Drain (D)
                  │
            Flat face toward you
</div>

<table>
  <tr><th>IRLZ44N Pin</th><th>Label</th><th>Connects To</th></tr>
  <tr><td><b>Left</b></td><td><b>Gate (G)</b></td><td>100Ω resistor from ESP32 GPIO 2 + 10kΩ resistor to GND</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>Center</b></td><td><b>Drain (D)</b></td><td>One end of TX coil + one leg of tuning capacitor</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>Right</b></td><td><b>Source (S)</b></td><td>Common GND</td></tr>
</table>

