<h3>3.3 Wire Connection Table</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>From</th><th>To</th><th>Wire / Component</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
  <tr><td>ESP32 GPIO 2</td><td>100Ω resistor</td><td>Jumper wire</td><td>Signal path</td></tr>
  <tr><td>100Ω resistor</td><td>Gate of IRLZ44N</td><td>Resistor lead</td><td>⛔ Never skip this resistor!</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Gate of IRLZ44N</td><td>GND</td><td>10kΩ resistor</td><td>Pull-down — keeps MOSFET OFF during boot</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Source of IRLZ44N</td><td>GND</td><td>Thick wire</td><td>Use 18–22 AWG for power handling</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Drain of IRLZ44N</td><td>Coil End 1 + Cap Leg 1</td><td>Solder joint</td><td>All three joined together</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Coil End 2</td><td>+V of external supply</td><td>Thick wire</td><td>Power feed</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Cap Leg 2</td><td>GND</td><td>Wire</td><td>Completes the LC tank</td></tr>
  <tr><td>External PSU (−)</td><td>GND</td><td>Thick wire</td><td>Common ground</td></tr>
  <tr><td>ESP32 GND</td><td>GND</td><td>Jumper wire</td><td>Must connect to same ground</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Battery (+)</td><td>Filament LED (+ side)</td><td>~15 cm wire</td><td>RX loop — keep ~10 cm diameter</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Filament LED (− side)</td><td>Battery (−)</td><td>~15 cm wire</td><td>RX loop — closes the circuit</td></tr>
</table>
</section>

<!-- ====== 4. COIL & CAPACITOR TABLES ====== -->
<section>
<h2>4. Coil &amp; Capacitor Selection Tables</h2>

<h3>4.1 Wire Gauge Reference</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>AWG</th><th>Diameter (mm)</th><th>Resistance (Ω/m)</th><th>Current Rating</th><th>Suitability</th></tr>
  <tr><td><b>18</b> ⭐</td><td>1.024</td><td>0.021</td><td>~3.5 A</td><td><b>Excellent</b> — lowest loss, best for 12W</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>20</b> ⭐</td><td>0.812</td><td>0.033</td><td>~2.5 A</td><td><b>Excellent</b> — best balance, easy to wind</td></tr>
  <tr><td>22</td><td>0.644</td><td>0.053</td><td>~1.7 A</td><td>Good — works fine up to 8W</td></tr>
  <tr><td>24</td><td>0.511</td><td>0.084</td><td>~1.2 A</td><td>OK — use up to 5–6W</td></tr>
  <tr><td>26</td><td>0.405</td><td>0.134</td><td>~0.8 A</td><td>Fair — higher loss, lower power</td></tr>
  <tr><td>30+</td><td>&lt;0.255</td><td>&gt;0.339</td><td>&lt;0.3 A</td><td>Poor — too resistive for &gt;1W</td></tr>
</table>

